{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:136-143` computes shrimp food demand with `grazing_access_factor`, but `update_condition()` recomputes `target_food_g` at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:267-273` without that same factor. That means a colony that eats its full accessible ration is still treated as partially unsatiated whenever grazing access is below 1.0, which is the default case. The result is a systematic condition/reproduction/maturation penalty in otherwise healthy tanks. Reuse the exact access-adjusted demand basis from feeding when deriving the food-factor target.","rationale":"This is scientific-core behavior, not just UI polish: it biases the new stage model toward chronically under-conditioned shrimp under normal substrate settings."},{"body":"`PlayerAction::AddShrimp` in `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:691-693` only increments `adult.count`. With the new stage-aware state, that bypasses the empty-stage seeding/merge logic in `StageCohort::receive_entrants()` (`crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs:97-123`). If the adult cohort had previously dropped to zero after poor conditions, newly added adults inherit the stale `adult.condition_index` from the dead cohort instead of starting from fresh state, so purchased shrimp can arrive effectively sick for no biological reason. Adding shrimp should go through cohort seeding/averaging rather than mutating the count directly.","rationale":"This is a user-visible correctness bug introduced by the new per-stage condition semantics."},{"body":"The snapshot compatibility story is incomplete. `TankSnapshotRepr` requires `total_shrimp_count` and `sub_adult_count` with no defaults (`crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:112-117`), but `normalize_snapshot_object()` only rewrites chemistry aliases (`crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:206-215`). `tank_tui` then deserializes snapshots directly via `serde_json::from_value()` (`crates/tank_tui/src/api_client.rs:112-113`). A newer client talking to a pre-stage server payload that only has `adult_shrimp_count`/`juveniles_count` will fail to parse snapshots instead of defaulting `sub_adult_count` to 0 and recomputing the total. Add serde defaults or explicit normalization for the new shrimp-stage fields.","rationale":"The bead explicitly calls for backward-compatible population summaries; mixed-version API/TUI use is currently broken by the new required snapshot fields."}],"summary":"Reviewed the shrimp stage-structure work across `biology.rs`, `shrimp.rs`, `save.rs`, `snapshot.rs`, API/TUI snapshot consumers, and related tests. `cargo test -p tank_core --test shrimp_population` and `cargo test -p tank_core --test save_load` both passed, but I still found three actionable issues: an access-factor mismatch in condition scoring, `AddShrimp` bypassing stage-state initialization, and missing backward compatibility for older snapshot payloads."}